1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,860
How can he just abandon everything

3
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,220
to go train in seclusion on his Seven-Color Holy Light?

4
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:33,480
I don't like Michael either.

5
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:36,540
Yeah, I really hate him. I want him to lose completely.

6
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,460
I'll restate my opinion.

7
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,340
Leo winning the Individual Title is certainly important.

8
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,700
But isn't the Jianghai Team's
Group Championship important too?

9
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:48,060
No distractions. No distractions.

10
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,460
The hardest hurdle is the Mental one.

11
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:54,300
If he said that to me, I wouldn't be scared.

12
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:55,740
What do you mean,

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,180
having a ghost living inside of your body?

14
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:00,060
Even if there is one, it'd just be another Chuck!

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,500
Episode 35

16
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,340
Chuck, the Tournament is almost here.

17
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,220
You can't keep being like this.

18
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:34,140
Your Health comes first.

19
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,610
Son, what do you actually want to eat?

20
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,820
Tell your Dad.

21
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:46,620
I want your Fish Head Casserole.

22
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,500
Ah, you want the Fish Head Casserole?

23
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,900
Don't you want some Spicy Boiled Fish too?

24
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,720
That works too.

25
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:56,220
Huh?

26
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:29,270
This is the most trendy piece right now.

27
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,700
No, no.

28
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,620
I want the most conservative clothes in your store.

29
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,500
Conservative?

30
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,300
Sis, what are you buying?

31
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,140
I want to get a new Yo-Yo string.

32
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,580
Can I?

33
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,500
No problem.

34
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,340
Then... can I also add a finger guard?

35
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:07,740
No problem.

36
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:11,580
It seems I'm out of maintenance oil, too.

37
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,500
Then buy it.

38
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:17,340
What about your Tooth Fund?

39
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,660
I've already thought it through.

40
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,540
The Tournament is about to start.

41
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,940
What do I need a Tooth Fund for now?

42
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,820
Wow, great! Mickey, you should have done this earlier.

43
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:32,220
Then I won't hold back.

44
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,100
I want maintenance oil, cleaning spray...

45
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:38,940
a new crystal Yo-Yo pouch, and a jewelry-style Yo-Yo case!

46
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,860
Also some gloves, and finger sleeves!

47
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:44,000
"Bankrupt"

48
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,100
No way!

49
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,860
Only $1 left.

50
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,260
Ah!

51
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,660
Ah, I've been knocking for ages.

52
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,070
Why did you just open the door now?

53
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,540
Sorry, I didn't hear.

54
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:01,730
What else do you need?

55
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:04,380
I've been thinking a lot.

56
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,780
and I think I still need to remind you once more.

57
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,830
Please mind your Mental State.

58
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,540
I know. Bye.

59
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:19,260
Remember, this is the key to your victory.

60
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,100
Alright, I'm leaving.

61
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,740
This is his 5th time today.

62
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,100
No Grandpa, this is his 6th time now.

63
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,630
I used to feel the exact same way when I was young.

64
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:52,860
I rolled over to my left side
and felt my heart uncomfortable.

65
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,260
The beating sound was strange.

66
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,660
So I turned to the right.

67
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,580
My right hand quickly went numb.

68
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:01,500
Like it had been anesthetized.

69
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,380
So I propped up my pillow.

70
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,600
But then my neck felt uncomfortable.

71
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,140
I removed the pillow, and then my head felt dizzy.

72
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:13,020
I thought maybe the magnetic field is wrong.

73
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,420
So I turned 360 degrees in bed

74
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,860
in different directions.

75
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:19,000
You are like a compass.

76
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,220
What happened in the end?

77
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:23,100
I don't even know if I fell asleep.

78
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,980
Seemed like I was just drowsy.

79
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,380
But when I woke up,

80
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:30,300
I found my head at the foot of the bed.

81
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:33,180
my feet propped up high against the wall.

82
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,540
I was so tired I felt numb.

83
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:38,940
Oh no!

84
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
That's an egg!

85
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,740
You must have been distracted.

86
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,060
You put an egg instead of your Yo-Yo in your bag.

87
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:46,620
Raw or boiled?

88
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,060
All you think about is eating.

89
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,900
Alright, alright, stop gloating over my misfortune!

90
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,300
Mark's going to scold me again later.

91
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:55,740
What for?

92
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Mark!

93
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:59,100
Hey Mark, what kind of shoes are you wearing?

94
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,310
This might become

95
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,370
the most trendy look this year.

96
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,670
Hey, Popcorn.

97
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,620
Since when did you start talking so ladylike?

98
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:11,580
Exactly.

99
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,980
I was used to you being so carefree.

100
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,420
Suddenly becoming so gentle,

101
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:17,820
I find it scary.

102
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:23,100
What's wrong with everyone lately?

103
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:24,540
I pondered over it all night.

104
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,940
and realized everyone has caught a sickness.

105
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,340
What? A sickness?

106
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,260
What sickness?

107
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:33,160
Tournament Anxiety Syndrome.

108
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:35,100
Syndrome?

109
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,060
Right.

110
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,900
Acting out of character is its main symptom.

111
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,300
For instance, Insomnia,

112
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,700
Changes in appetite,

113
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:48,060
Confusion, Absent-mindedness,

114
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,900
Looking around restlessly, even silence.

115
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,780
Severe cases may even hallucinate.

116
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,850
Like having no sense of time, etc.

117
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,570
Huh?

118
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,500
As for losing the ability to calculate,

119
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:04,380
that probably means it's terminal and incurable.

120
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,740
Ah, it's over.

121
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:10,140
What do we do then?

122
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:12,060
The best way is

123
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:14,910
to take what's causing you nervousness

124
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,380
and forget it completely.

125
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,780
What Shawn said makes sense!

126
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:20,700
The Tournament is next week!

127
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:24,060
But the closer we get to the end,
the more we need to relax.

128
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,940
Now the intensity of Training no longer matters.

129
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,380
What matters is

130
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,820
to maintain a good mindset.

131
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,260
So when the Competition comes,

132
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,700
we can perform at our best.

133
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,100
Well tomorrow is Sunday.

134
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,810
Let's all go on an Outing together.

135
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,260
Come in.

136
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:58,140
Mom, you wanted to see me?

137
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,020
Have a seat.

138
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,520
Your Dad called.

139
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,140
Asking about your recent studies.

140
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,020
Everything's fine! All my grades are good.

141
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:19,260
What do you mean 'fine'? Take a look for yourself.

142
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,140
You only scored 97 in Chemistry.

143
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:26,460
That's the second highest in the class.

144
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:31,260
Then who's first? Are you content being second?

145
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,020
Teddy, I've told you before,

146
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,350
In our Family, ever since your Grandfather's generation...

147
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,300
He's always been a leading figure in the Chemical Industry.

148
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,180
Not to mention a factory with over 2000 people,

149
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,100
is all run by your Dad.

150
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,020
Even in the entire Chemical Industry,

151
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:53,340
Nobody dares to underestimate your Father.
What does he rely on?

152
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,700
He relies on true talent and practical knowledge.

153
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,620
With grades like yours,

154
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,540
how can you possibly take over your Father's legacy?

155
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,380
Mom, I already know all this.

156
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:07,260
If you know, why did you still get such a score?

157
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,660
But you can't possibly expect me

158
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,100
to get a Perfect score every time.

159
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:13,020
As the old saying goes,

160
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,870
"Even monkeys fall from trees."

161
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:18,780
Quiet! Where did you learn to be so glib?

162
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,140
Teddy.

163
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,990
Your Father and I have placed

164
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,460
all our hopes on you.

165
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:29,820
We hope you can get into a prestigious University.

166
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:33,180
so you can study abroad for further education in the future.

167
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,500
Your whole Family is counting on you to bring them glory.

168
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:41,820
What era is this?
Still talking about bringing glory to the Family?

169
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,220
Enough! This is not up to you.

170
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,620
I've discussed it with your Father.

171
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,510
We've decided to transfer you to another School.

172
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:50,460
What? Transfer?

173
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:53,820
Yes. The Chemistry program at
Jianghai High School is too weak.

174
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:56,220
You simply can't build a solid foundation there.

175
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,620
So how could you possibly study abroad?

176
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,060
So we've decided

177
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,460
to transfer you to Saint Qiao High School.

178
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,320
What? Saint Qiao High School!

179
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:32,700
Give me a small knife.

180
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,980
Matthew, are the skewers ready yet?

181
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,020
Ready, ready.

182
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:43,630
I'll go check again.

183
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:48,100
Matthew, I'm dying of thirst. Bring a drink over.

184
00:13:48,150 --> 00:13:50,280
Oh, thanks.

185
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:54,750
Monica.

186
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:55,740
I'll go check on the chicken wings.

187
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:56,940
Go ahead.

188
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Wait!

189
00:13:58,430 --> 00:13:59,580
What do you want?

190
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,570
How can you stand someone with such a temper?

191
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:03,900
I really admire you.

192
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:07,710
Hehe, I'm happy to.

193
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,180
Ah.

194
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,180
I like this.

195
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:26,460
I like this too.

196
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:33,180
I like this the most!

197
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,900
So awesome!

198
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,300
Let me do it. Let me do it.

199
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,220
You guys take care of your stuff, it's fine.

200
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:45,480
Matthew, let's go.

201
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,350
What's up with Teddy?

202
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,600
You just criticize him a little,

203
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:56,000
and he won't even join Group Activities.

204
00:14:56,810 --> 00:14:57,950
He's become so narrow-minded.

205
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,980
His Mom said his Dad is coming back today.

206
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,380
Do you all know

207
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:07,260
his Dad only comes back a few times a Year.

208
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:08,700
Every time he comes back,

209
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,100
Teddy spends a lot time with him.

210
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:16,380
Ah, Teddy really has no luck with food.

211
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:20,220
Well, one less person means more for the rest of us.

212
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,750
His share is mine.

213
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:25,020
Chuck, I really admire you.

214
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:26,460
Your Dad feeds you

215
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:27,900
so much good food,

216
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,340
and you still haven't had enough?

217
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:33,660
Ah, you just don't understand
the hunger of a starving man.

218
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,100
All that stuff my Dad makes,

219
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,020
I'm almost sick of it.

220
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:38,940
Then stop pretending to be starving.

221
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,280
Then maybe it's a starving man who
doesn't understand a full man's boredom.

222
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,860
How is it? Any catch?

223
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:30,780
Not yet.

224
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,030
Looks like I need to change spots.

225
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,940
Shawn, fishing is all about patience.

226
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:43,260
I think it's more about fate.

227
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:46,620
I'm off, won't bother you guys.

228
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:50,940
Ignore him.

229
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:52,380
He's always like this, all Mystical.

230
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:53,340
It's fine.

231
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,260
Stalemate.

232
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:18,780
C'mon.

233
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:20,220
Chariot to the 7th rank.

234
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:23,580
Will that work?

235
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,030
Up to you.

236
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,780
Alright, I'll listen to you. Chariot to the 7th.

237
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:33,660
Sorry, sorry. That's Checkmate.

238
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:37,500
Doesn't count, doesn't count. He told me to do it.

239
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,940
You made that move yourself.

240
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,300
This is outrageous!

241
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,180
What a foul mouth!

242
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,710
Rematch, rematch, rematch!

243
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Thank you.

244
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:57,180
Shawn, you're coming back empty-handed again.

245
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,580
Looks like your trip was a waste.

246
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,940
I just haven't caught the big fish I'm waiting for.

247
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:05,820
There are so many fish in the river.

248
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,740
How do you know which big fish
is the one you're waiting for?

249
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:12,060
It's a feeling, an intuition.

250
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:15,420
A kind of illusion. You get it?

251
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,300
It's something you can't quite put into words, right?

252
00:18:18,490 --> 00:18:19,740
Yeah, exactly!

253
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:25,230
I fish to cultivate patience, to cultivate calm.

254
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:30,300
Once you relax, your heart naturally quiets down.

255
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,220
In that state the inspiration,

256
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:37,980
just like the big fish I'm waiting for.

257
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,860
it will naturally surface.

258
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:45,180
That must be a fish that talks to itself.

259
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:47,950
Whatever fish it is,

260
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,460
As long as it ends up in my Dad's stew pot,

261
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:51,660
it all tastes the same.

262
00:18:55,470 --> 00:18:56,220
This is just unreasonable!

263
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:57,660
Did you enjoy fishing in the US too?

264
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:02,460
Occasionally, But usually it was by the sea.

265
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,510
When will you return to the US?

266
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:09,180
Next year.

267
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:11,580
I definitely have to go back next year.

268
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:25,470
I'm going back to participate in next Year's

269
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,900
American Chinese Youth Yo-Yo Competition.

270
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,820
Why are you so determined to go back

271
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:30,780
for that Competition?

272
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,570
Because I need to find the things I lost,

273
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:42,300
and take them back again.

274
00:20:49,380 --> 00:20:50,940
Mini, come help!

275
00:20:52,060 --> 00:20:52,860
